  "intro": "Source: Lecture notes 10/22, pages 1 to 3, with one added section on splitting for the past exam's Question 2B.<br>After this reading you can:<br>• Describe what a spectrometer does: light in, specific frequencies absorbed, structure out<br>• Explain why nuclei in a magnetic field have two energy states and how the gap depends on the field<br>• Explain shielding: the field of the electrons subtracts from the external field, and the nucleus feels the net field<br>• Count the 1H and 13C signals of a molecule by finding the different environments<br>• Use the n + 1 rule to say what a septet means",
