       [
        "Why does a sample absorb only specific frequencies of light and not all of them?",
        "Absorption moves something from a lower energy state to a higher one, and those states have fixed energies. Only light whose energy hν equals the gap ΔE can be absorbed. Because the gaps depend on the structure, the absorbed frequencies report on the structure."
       ]
