       [
        "Why must two chairs with different energies be diastereomers?",
        "Identical structures have identical energies, and so do enantiomers, since mirror images contain the same distances and interactions. If two chairs of the same molecule differ in energy they are neither identical nor mirror images. Stereoisomers that are not mirror images are diastereomers."
       ]
