        "Carbon is the least electronegative of C, N and O, so it is the atom least able to stabilize a negative charge. The methyl anion is therefore the least stable of the anions and the most eager to share its electron pair with a proton. Its conjugate acid, methane, is correspondingly the weakest acid."
