        "In the synthesis, why does the deuterium end up on the middle carbon and nowhere else?",
        "Only the carbon bonded to magnesium (or lithium) is carbanion-like and able to take a D from D2O. That is the carbon that held the bromine, and HBr placed the bromine on the middle carbon of propene. Every other hydrogen in the molecule is an ordinary alkane C-H and is not touched."
