        "Why does ethanol not react with {{HS-}} when bromoethane does?",
        "The leaving group would be {{HO-}}, a strong base whose conjugate acid (water) has {{pKa}} 15.7. A strong base is high in energy as a free anion, so the transition state that begins to form it is too high. Bromide is a very weak base and leaves easily."
