        "Why is tert-butoxide a strong base but a poor nucleophile?",
        "Taking a proton only requires reaching a hydrogen on the outside of a molecule, and the bulk around oxygen does not prevent that. Attacking carbon requires getting to the crowded back side of the C-LG bond, and the three methyl groups of tert-butoxide collide with the substituents there."
