       [
        "Why do SN1 and E1 always appear together?",
        "They share the slow step and the intermediate. Once the carbocation exists, it can be attacked at carbon (substitution) or lose a neighbouring proton (elimination), and both are fast. Conditions such as temperature only shift the ratio between the two."
       ]
