        "In {{E2}} the base must pull off a hydrogen from an ordinary C-H bond while the leaving group is still attached, so it has to be strong enough to drive that step. In {{E1}} the leaving group has already gone, and the hydrogen next to a carbocation is so acidic that even water can take it."
