        "The Zaitsev rule compares the stability of alkenes that can actually form. If the hydrogen needed for the more substituted alkene cannot get anti to the leaving group, the transition state for that path lacks the orbital overlap it needs and is far too high in energy. The reaction then goes through the hydrogen that can line up."
